Subject: [PATCH] Keep RDMA allocation and stream ownership with Torch

The DeepEP wrapper owns the RDMA allocation through its DLPack capsule (or
Torch tensor). Proxies borrow its address and must not free it during stop:
that otherwise double-frees the allocation when Buffer is released.

Dispatch/combine also record tensor lifetimes on the communication stream.
Those tensors can outlive Buffer.destroy(), so destroying a private native
stream leaves the caching allocator recording events on an invalid handle.
Use a high-priority PyTorch pool stream and pass its borrowed handle to the
native runtime. Preserve record_stream and all post-destroy GPU checks.

Applies to UCCL 18b588a048a3a3fe3d4bd60aa5678c66e284df31.

diff --git a/ep/bench/buffer.py b/ep/bench/buffer.py
index 1fd4a24..cc95a25 100644
--- a/ep/bench/buffer.py
+++ b/ep/bench/buffer.py
@@ -179,9 +179,13 @@ class Buffer:
         self.low_latency_mode = low_latency_mode
         self.explicitly_destroy = explicitly_destroy
         self._next_low_latency_combine_buffer = None
+        # Pool-owned streams remain valid for tensors recorded on them even
+        # after this Buffer is destroyed.
+        self._comm_stream = torch.cuda.Stream(device=device_index, priority=-1)
         self.runtime = ep.Buffer(
             self.rank,
             self.group_size,
+            int(self._comm_stream.cuda_stream),
             num_nvl_bytes,
             num_rdma_bytes,
             low_latency_mode,
@@ -662,14 +666,7 @@ class Buffer:
         Returns:
             stream: the communication stream.
         """
-        ts = self.runtime.get_comm_stream()
-        if isinstance(ts, torch.Stream):
-            return torch.cuda.Stream(
-                stream_id=ts.stream_id,
-                device_index=ts.device_index,
-                device_type=ts.device_type,
-            )
-        return torch.cuda.ExternalStream(int(ts))
+        return self._comm_stream
 
     def get_local_buffer_tensor(
         self,
